  {
   "verse_number": 3,
   "source_text_master": [
    "yā’re dekhe tā’re kahe dante tṛṇa dhari’",
    "‘āmāre kiniyā laha, bala gaurahari 3’",
    "eta bali’ nityānanda bhūme gaḓi’ yāya",
    "sonāra parbata yena dhūlāte loṭāya 4"
   ],
   "translations": [
    {
     "language_code": "eng",
     "text": [
      "Holding a straw in His teeth, He calls out to whomever He sees, “Please purchase Me by calling out ‘Gaurahari!’ ” Speaking in this way, Nityānanda Prabhu rolls on the ground, appearing like a golden mountain tumbling in the dust."
     ]
    }
   ],
